sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 82.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg linear dispersion is calibrated so argmax σ(k) = 41.016 µm at age 0 Ma (Du = 10.659 µm², Dv = 191.861 µm², ratio 18). Analytic versus numeric growth-rate Pearson r = 0.9923 (RMSE 0.051). The axisymmetric Galerkin fit to the ocellus card has Pearson r = 0.9997. The scale helper returns 100/width (µm per px, 0.9009) but callers treat it as px per µm, so the 41 µm carrier carries only 0.14% of the wave amplitude and the dark-ring pitch is reported as 82.14 µm instead of about 67 µm. σ(96 µm) = -0.490 (mandarina contrast damped) and the Du = Dv ablation growth rate is -1.315. Overall 82.5/100 (faithfulness 80.7, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 3132697 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 d768ef9b85c6ae76a7f674e668a292fc07b7b7d90eccba040817d9e558195de4 (sha256 d768ef9b85c6ae76a7f674e668a292fc07b7b7d90eccba040817d9e558195de4), spec_fingerprint 900e8c4cd551803050526b60486b8aa4c0338d7c662a7b9812395080ca4e0324. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 900e8c4cd551803050526b60486b8aa4c0338d7c662a7b9812395080ca4e0324; artifact_sha256: d768ef9b85c6ae76a7f674e668a292fc07b7b7d90eccba040817d9e558195de4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/bombyx_mori_adult_cc0.jpg=76144516fb810472..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/bombyx_mori_ocellus_specimen.jpg=2adf51228d2da684..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=0a11d56294fb484c..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=08ab9cb9580075e6..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=9e4a322221a85be7...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Yamaguchi et al. 2013: periodic Wnt1 expression generates Bombyx larval twin spots. | Turing 1952 and Gierer & Meinhardt 1972: a finite wavelength is selected when the inhibitor diffuses farther than the activator.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian with a = 0.058, b = 0.94, Dv/Du = 18, rescaled so λ_c = 41 µm. | Axisymmetric Galerkin sideband fitted to the canonical ocellus card. | Predecessor contrast σ(2π/96 µm) < 0 < σ(2π/41 µm) at 0 Ma. No successor chronospecies.; transfer_boundary: Wnt1 twin spots in the source paper are segment-scale. The 41 µm figure is this slot's cellular detail scale, not a length Yamaguchi measured.; does_not_claim: That 41 µm or 96 µm was measured on a fossil or on Bombyx mandarina. | That the Pass-1 ring pitch of 82.14 µm is the card's true pitch. The unit conversion is inverted. | A pixel-fitted nonlinear 2D spot field.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'measure_scale_bar returns micrometres per pixel (100/width) while fit_galerkin and segment_card treat the value as pixels per micrometre. Return width/100, re-place the 41 µm carrier, and recompute the dark-ring pitch.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Replace the constant-gray ablation panel with a field evolved at Du = Dv from the same seeded noise, and keep the numeric growth rate σ < 0.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Emit the Kolmogorov-Smirnov p-value as its own measurement (value not equal to the reference) alongside D, Pearson r, and RMSE.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Re-render the GIF after the scale correction and re-score computer-vision similarity against the ocellus card.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.825"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

